IN LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOHARA, KIYOTSUNA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIWATA TOYOAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OZAKI DAISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SADANOBU JIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYOHARA KIYOTSUNA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIWATA, TOYOAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OZAKI, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SADANOBU, JIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOHARA, KIYOTSUNA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A resin composition comprising a blend of a crystalline polyimide, e.g., one represented by formula (1) wherein R1 represents an optionally substituent, divalent, C2-30, aromatic or aliphatic, organic group; and Ar1 represents an optionally substituted, C6-45 aromatic group, with a thermoplastic polyester. The resin composition is excellent in mechanical properties, e.g., high modulus, and in flowability and heat resistance. It is suitable for use in electronic parts capable of surface mounting.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une composition de résine comprenant un mélange d'un polyimide cristallin représenté par la formule (I) dans laquelle R1 représente un groupe organique, aromatique ou aliphatique, en C2-30, divalent, éventuellement substitué ; et Ar1 représente un groupe aromatique en C6-45, éventuellement substitué avec un polyester thermoplastique. Cette composition de résine présente d'excellentes propriétés mécaniques telles qu'un module d'élasticité élevé, une excellente aptitude à l'écoulement et une excellente résistance à la chaleur. Cette composition est appropriée pour être utilisée dans des pièces électroniques pouvant se monter en surface.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>